{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>The two great luminaries.</b> This means: both of them were great, but one was greater than the other, as it is written: את המאור הגדול. And our Rabbis expounded: at first they were created equal in greatness, and the moon complained and was diminished, and the sun remained in its greatness, because it heard its disgrace and did not reply. And that is what we say: those who are insulted and do not insult back, who hear their disgrace and do not reply — concerning them Scripture says: ואוהביו כצאת השמש בגבורתו, like the sun, which heard its disgrace and did not reply, and was thereby made great. And also in the Yozer for Shabbat, there are those whose text reads: ראה והקטין צורת הלבנה, and its meaning is thus: the Holy One, blessed be He, saw that she complained and diminished her. And for those whose text reads ראה והתקין, the explanation is thus: the Holy One, blessed be He, saw that the nations of the world were destined to go astray after the sun and make it idolatry, so He arose and established the form of the moon, to show them that the sun is not a god — for behold there is another sun, as fitting and beautiful as it."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:15:46.228926777Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}